<title>USA: Analysts Intl gets 3M contract.</title>
<headline>Analysts Intl gets 3M contract.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Analysts International Corp said Thursday it won a contract to help Minnesota Mining &amp; Manufacturing Co with Year 2000 software compliance in the company's financial systems area.</p>
<p>Under the contract Analysts International is responsible for providing a software conversion team for 3M's financial systems. The value of the contract was not disclosed.</p>
<p>The arrival of 2000 will require a massive computer-code overhaul for most computer systems to keep them functioning accurately after December 31, 1999.</p>
<p>The 3M project is one of several being carried out by Analysts International, which provides a variety of computer software services.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
